  "card": "Adds systemd hardening and sandboxing directives to the example bitcoind service unit in contrib/init, including syscall filters, namespace restrictions, an empty capability set, and socket address family limits. Deployments relying on the provided unit currently run without defense-in-depth process sandboxing, leaving unnecessary system interfaces accessible if the daemon process is compromised. The PR also changes the ExecStartPre prefix so permission adjustments on the config directory succeed under the new restrictions.",
